  "description": "Reid Method 2 | 20\" BMX bike\nTake your BMX riding to the next level with the Reid Bikes Method 2, a tough and capable 20\" BMX bike designed for riders aged 7+ years. Built for developing skills, tricks and confidence, it's ready for BMX parks, pump tracks, street riding and everyday sessions.\nThe tried-and-tested Hi-Ten steel frame features modern BMX geometry and predictable handling, giving young riders a solid platform for learning manuals, jumps, whips and other BMX skills. The seat-stay mounted U-brake and two-finger brake lever provide reliable control for technical riding and tricks.\nBuilt to handle demanding BMX sessions, the Method 2 features a forged alloy stem and seat clamp, 36-hole double-wall rims and a durable KMC chain. The upgraded 3-piece crankset, 25T x 9T gearing and cassette hub provide a strong and reliable drivetrain for riders looking to progress.\nFinished in black with bold red detailing, the Reid Bikes Method 2 combines BMX-ready durability with a clean, modern look. It's built to help young riders push their skills further and enjoy every session.\nWho is the Reid Bikes Method 2 for?\nThe Method 2 BMX is ideal for:\n\nRiders aged 7+ years progressing their BMX skills\nYoung riders ready to develop more advanced BMX techniques\nBMX parks, pump tracks and street riding\nRiders practising manuals, jumps, whips and tricks\nBMX riders looking for a durable, performance-focused bike\nRiders wanting a 3-piece crank and cassette hub",
